  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "NOR as a universal gate"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "NOT: tie both inputs of a NOR together: $\\overline{A + A} = \\overline{A}$. OR: NOR followed by a NOR-inverter (2 gates). AND: invert each input with a NOR, then NOR the results: $\\overline{\\overline{A}+\\overline{B}} = AB$ (3 gates). Notice the pattern is the mirror image of NAND."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "NOT: 1 NOR"
    },
    {
     "en": "OR: 2 NORs"
    },
    {
     "en": "AND: 3 NORs"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "With NOR gates it is the mirror image: one gives NOT, two give OR and three give AND.",
    "kn": "ನಾರ್ ದ್ವಾರಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇದು ಪ್ರತಿಬಿಂಬ: ಒಂದು ನಾಟ್, ಎರಡು ಆರ್, ಮೂರು ಆಂಡ್."
   }
  },
